{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>From HaShem, a snare</b> — [verses 24–25] are joined. \"His steps\" — the steps he strides to walk." "<b>And a man</b> — does not understand the time of his going, until HaShem leads him and settles him. \"From Him are a man's steps,\" and He places a snare in his path for whomever will swallow — and he eats holy food, and after he is snared he vows vows to bring a fool's offering, he escapes the snare and swallows from your provisions, they will mutter blood like he is swallowed.\nn: The entire second comment is textually obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The string 'ילע מן בלעיך' is uncertain and may be corrupt; the final clause 'יעלעו דם כמו יבלע' is also difficult."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:54.620849540Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}